# ops.yaml — the operations channel, and who may broadcast from it.
#
# Optional. Without this file there is no ops agent, no ops channel and no
# announce tool: the feature is absent rather than half-present.
#
# THIS CHANNEL MUST BE PRIVATE. Membership is the authorisation — anyone in it
# can broadcast to every tenant channel. That is deliberate, and it is the same
# reasoning that makes channel membership the perimeter for tenants: one
# control rather than two that drift apart, and adding an operator is a Slack
# invite rather than a config change and a deploy.
#
# It only works because the channel is private, so the tool asks Slack on every
# call and refuses if the channel is public. In a public channel joining is one
# click and membership would grant nothing.
channelId: C00000000OPS
